12
00:56:34,285 --> 00:56:40,285
Abandon is a 2002 American psychological thriller drama film written
and directed by Stephen Gaghan in his directorial debut.

13
01:01:17,142 --> 01:01:23,142
It follows a college student (Katie Holmes) whose boyfriend
(Charlie Hunnam) disappeared two years previously.

14
01:05:59,999 --> 01:06:05,999
Despite being set at an American university, much of the movie was filmed
in Montreal, Quebec at McGill University's McConnell Hall.

15
01:10:42,857 --> 01:10:48,857
It is based on the book Adams Fall by Sean Desmond.

16
01:15:25,714 --> 01:15:31,714
The book was re-titled Abandon for the movie tie-in paperback printing.

17
01:20:08,571 --> 01:20:14,571
The film co-stars Zooey Deschanel, Gabrielle Union, and Melanie Lynskey, with Benjamin Bratt
playing the detective who is investigating the boyfriend's disappearance.

18
01:24:51,428 --> 01:24:57,428
It was a critical and commercial failure.

19
01:29:34,285 --> 01:29:40,285
The film explores themes of dancer, nightmare, alcohol, detective, college.

20
01:34:17,142 --> 01:34:23,142
The tone is intense and emotional and mind_bending.
